# [Send a Decision request]($heading.id('decision'))

`POST /v1/systemone` accepts a JSON object and returns scored labels for the
requested questions. The loaded model must support Decision. Use the
[worked request]($link.page('llmd/developer-guide/ask-structured-questions').ref('send-a-decision-request'))
or copy one from [Configure launch]($link.page('llmd/user-guide/configure-launch/2026.11.3').unsafeRef('send-a-decision-request')).

| Request field | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `state` | String or object, required | Input shared by every question. The server renders an object as compact JSON. |
| `questions` | Object, required | Maps question IDs to definitions. IDs must be nonempty and exclude the colon character. Send dependencies before the questions that reference them. |
| `instructions` | String, optional | System instructions shared by all questions. |
| `ask` | Array of question IDs, optional | Select the questions to answer. Include every dependency of the selected questions. Omitting this field asks all questions. |
| `model` | String, optional | The endpoint uses the model already loaded by LLMD. The field can be omitted. |

# [Question kinds and dependencies]($heading.id('question-kinds-and-dependencies'))

Each question requires `kind` and a string `instructions`. Its `criteria`
describe the possible labels.

| `kind` | `criteria` | Successful `label` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `choice` | Required object mapping labels to descriptions. Use a string or `null` for each description. | One of the object keys. |
| `noul` | Optional object with descriptions under `"true"` and `"false"`. | The string `"true"` or `"false"`. |
| `score` | Required array of scale labels, such as `["low","medium","high"]`. | One of the supplied strings. |

Use `depends_on` to supply a list of earlier question IDs whose available
labels become context. Use `ask_if` to gate execution. Its keys are earlier
question IDs and its values are arrays of acceptable labels. Every named
question must return a label in its corresponding array for the question to run.

# [Read the response]($heading.id('decision-response'))

`answers` maps question IDs to results. This example asks only for `animal`
with `"ask": ["animal"]`. Token IDs, scores and counts are illustrative.

```=html
<fieldset class="decision-response">
  <legend>Select an underlined field in the JSON to inspect it.</legend>
  <div class="decision-response-layout">
    <div class="command-shell">
      <span class="command-language icon-code">JSON · Decision response</span>
      <pre><code data-copy-label="Copy Decision response">{
  <span class="token property">"answers"</span>: {
    <span class="token property">"animal"</span>: {
      <label class="decision-key"><input type="radio" name="decision-field" value="label" aria-label="label" aria-controls="decision-label-note">"label"</label>: <span class="token string">"cat"</span>,
      <label class="decision-key"><input type="radio" name="decision-field" value="scores" aria-label="scores" aria-controls="decision-scores-note">"scores"</label>: [
        {<span class="token property">"label"</span>: <span class="token string">"cat"</span>, <span class="token property">"token_id"</span>: <span class="token number">7</span>,
         <span class="token property">"logprob"</span>: <span class="token number">-0.916291</span>, <span class="token property">"probability"</span>: <span class="token number">0.8</span>},
        {<span class="token property">"label"</span>: <span class="token string">"dog"</span>, <span class="token property">"token_id"</span>: <span class="token number">9</span>,
         <span class="token property">"logprob"</span>: <span class="token number">-2.302585</span>, <span class="token property">"probability"</span>: <span class="token number">0.2</span>}
      ],
      <label class="decision-key"><input type="radio" name="decision-field" value="prompt_contribution" aria-label="prompt_contribution" aria-controls="decision-contribution-note" checked>"prompt_contribution"</label>: <span class="token number">0.5</span>
    }
  },
  <span class="token property">"usage"</span>: {<span class="token property">"prompt_tokens"</span>: <span class="token number">48</span>, <span class="token property">"cached_tokens"</span>: <span class="token number">0</span>}
}
</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-annotation">
      <div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
        <div class="decision-field-note" id="decision-label-note" data-field="label">
          <strong><code>label</code></strong>
          <p>The winning label is <code>"cat"</code>. It has the highest probability among the offered labels.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision-field-note" id="decision-scores-note" data-field="scores">
          <strong><code>scores</code></strong>
          <p>Each entry names a label and its first <code>token_id</code>. <code>logprob</code> is that token’s log probability across the full vocabulary. <code>probability</code> is its share among the offered labels.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision-field-note" id="decision-contribution-note" data-field="prompt_contribution">
          <strong><code>prompt_contribution</code></strong>
          <p>The first tokens for cat and dog together account for half the probability mass. Cat’s share among those two labels is <code>0.4 / 0.5 = 0.8</code>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl class="decision-probabilities">
        <dt>Across the full vocabulary</dt>
        <dd><span aria-hidden="true" class="decision-bar" style="--cat: 40%; --offered: 50%"></span>Cat 40% · Dog 10% · Other tokens 50%</dd>
        <dt>Among the offered labels</dt>
        <dd><span aria-hidden="true" class="decision-bar" style="--cat: 80%; --offered: 100%"></span>Cat 80% · Dog 20%</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</fieldset>
```

`usage` totals prompt and cached tokens across the questions that ran.

## [Per-question outcomes]($heading.id('decision-outcomes'))

An HTTP 200 response can contain all three outcomes. Check each entry in `answers` before reading its label.

| Outcome | Fields in the entry | How to handle it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Answered | `label`, `scores`, `prompt_contribution` | Read the winning label and its score. |
| Skipped | `{"skipped":true}` | An `ask_if` condition was false. Continue without a label. |
| Failed | For example, `{"error":"prompt_too_long"}` | Handle this question’s error. Other entries can still contain answers. |

# [Limits and errors]($heading.id('decision-limits-and-errors'))

Per-question errors include `prompt_too_long`, `unsupported_chat_template`,
`resource_exhausted`, and `aborted`. An unsupported model or invalid request
returns HTTP 400 with a plain-text explanation.
For `ForwardDependency`, put the referenced question earlier in the JSON
object. For `DuplicateOptionToken`, choose labels whose first tokens differ.

LLMD revision `ca575167` limits the request body to 4 MiB, accepts 1–1,024
questions, and scores 2–16 options per question. Its Decision path is enabled
for the LFM3 model implementation. See the [Decision catalog]($link.page('llmd/user-guide/model-compatibility').unsafeRef('decision-checkpoints'))
for model and build evidence, and [Parallel work and Decision requests]($link.page('llmd/cli-reference/batching-and-memory').ref('parallel-work-and-decision-requests'))
for the per-request concurrency control `--systemone-window`.
